@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option Desk - Capability selection and access checks

component "Requested capability\noptional explicit provider" as need
component "Registry priority lists" as reg #C6E9C6
component "Option chain / rate / dividends\nYahoo candidate" as single
component "History / quote\nYahoo, then Alpha Vantage" as fallback
component "Provider checks\nmode + terms/rights + key + dependency" as gate
component "Available candidate\nreturn provider + skipped reasons" as available
component "No permitted candidate\nProviderUnavailable" as error
component "Imported snapshot\nsource + rights + field checks" as imp
need --> reg
reg --> single
reg --> fallback
single --> gate
fallback --> gate
gate --> available : allowed and available
gate --> error : none available
note bottom of reg
An explicit provider is strict by default.
Failure does not silently select a different provider.
end note
note bottom of gate
Demo mode refuses external providers.
Yahoo requires local-use acknowledgement.
A key is not proof of redistribution rights.
Alpha Vantage supplies history and quotes, not option chains.
end note
note bottom of imp
The import route does not resolve a live provider.
Its source and permission checks still apply.
end note

caption Sources: providers/__init__.py, providers/base.py, providers/yahoo.py and cli/chain.py. No provider quota or availability claim.
@enduml
